## 5. Failure Recovery & Edge Case Handling

| Symptom | Root Cause | Resolution Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Click intercepted or non-responsive** | Element covered by modal backdrop, sticky header, or animation overlay. | 1. Query `document.elementFromPoint(x, y)` to identify occluding node.<br>2. Dismiss overlay or call `element.scrollIntoView({ block: "center" })`.<br>3. Fall back to coordinate click `click_at(x, y)` or dispatch client click in `evaluate_script`. |
| **Snapshot UID Invalidated** | DOM re-rendered or client-side route changed dynamically. | Call `take_snapshot` to regenerate current element `uid` references before retrying action. |
| **Port Collision (EADDRINUSE)** | Lingering dev server process occupies required port. | Identify PID using `lsof -ti :<port>`, terminate process, or parse alternate port assigned in build tool stdout. |
| **Dev Server Unreachable (`ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED`)** | Server still compiling or bound strictly to `127.0.0.1` vs `0.0.0.0`. | Monitor background process log for `"Ready in X ms"`, sleep 1500ms, and retry connection. |
| **Hidden File Input (`display: none`)** | Modern UI proxies file selection via button or drag zone. | Supply the `uid` of the hidden `<input type="file">` directly to `upload_file`. The tool will populate the file list regardless of CSS visibility. |

